
             Here's what's in store for AmiQWK II and beyond.

     ----------------------------------------------------------------

    *   Operation in user defined screen mode.

    *   Proportional font support where appropriate.

    *   ANSI text display mode.

    *   Improved Text Display Routines.

    *   Routines to store, select, and steal taglines.

    *   Improved Reply handling.

    *   Ability to Move, Delete,  Rename,  ect.  mail  packets  from
        within AmiQWK.

    *   Large  replies  split  into  multiple  messages  with   user
        definable maximum message size.

    *   Information files. Information such  as  read/unread  status
        for each message, 'Bookmarks' ect. can be saved.

    *   Index file rebulder.

    *   Optional scroll bar for message text.

    *   Packet Information Window.

    *   CLI operation.

    *   Menus where appropriate.
 
    *   'IFF' style config file format.

    *   'Index' list (List of all messages in conference).

    *   Picklists for To: in replies.

    *   search functions.

    *   Sorting of Conference and Messages.

    *   Print message text.

    *   Save message text to file.
    
    *   'Request attached file' function.
    
    *   Add/Drop conferences.
    
    *   Message forwarding.

    *   Hypertext Help.

    *   Message marking (for save, print, etc.)

             And Much Much more....

